 tarly reading a book about  this dagger that states when aegon the  conqueror forged his seven kingdoms he  and his descendants would often decorate  their blades with dragonglass feeling a  kinship with the stone its blade is made  of valyrian steel and hilt that of  dragonglass the only two substances  known to kill white walkers in the  season trailers we've seen allison to  wield this blade and attack rhaenyra  with it it's a bit difficult to tell  what happens in the scene but my  prediction is she takes it off king  viserys who at this point will be much  more sick and attempts to stab the  princess this may be because one of  ranira's children cut out the eye of one  of hers ranira seems to be alongside her  father here who is showing her this  inscription further highlighting the  blade's importance notice at this point  rhaenyra is not wearing that valerian  steel necklace she received from her  uncle in episode 1 yet later in the  trailer she is in the season to come  trailer we get this added voiceover of  the king in this scene stating that the  quote burden of this knowledge is larger  than the throne the hand of the king  otto hightower skulks off to the side of  the great hall i'm wondering if this is  when prince damon returns from the  stepstones we'll see someone who could  be otto in this wide shot plus the  servant with the pillow looks to be the  same one who gives viserys his crown  during this tense confrontation take  note of prince damon here either in the  red keep or some brothel his hair  notably shorter than when we saw him at  the stepstones we'll find out that this  episode takes place roughly one year  after the events of episode 3. what i  want you to pay attention to is his  white shirt in the season ahead trailer  we see the king hold a dagger to his  brother telling him he's no conqueror  he's a plague these two seem to be alone  here in the great hall and the king  events his frustration now that his  brother must be seen as a hero even  though he went against his brother's  wishes there's not much we can pick out  here other than alison is no longer  pregnant in the year that passed she  would have given birth to her second of  four children helena past the skull of  valerian you can make out a figure  walking in the background the season  ahead trailer has a better shot of this  person and will later see a similarly  clothed rhaenyra running through the  streets with a shot of a drunk in the  background combine this with these  servants looking for someone it appears  rhaenyra has slipped out of the red keep  not wanting to be noticed perhaps it has  something to do with her uncle we'll see  him clad in a black cloak he too looks  as though he does not want to be  discovered the king puts on his crown  awaiting their rival of damon who also  wears a crown that of the stepstones in  the book corliss named him the king of  the narrow sea that patch of water  separating westeros from essos these  would be seas belonging to king viserys  so each men flaunting their crowns is  nothing but a glorified dick-swinging  contest i'm really curious why rhaenyra  is wearing her uncle's necklace here the  last we saw these two interact it could  have led to her death perhaps they've  made up or maybe rhaenyra just wants to  piss off her father returning to the  great hall is daemon holding  kragustrahar's hammer the same one the  crab feeder used to nail his victims to  driftwood the kingsguard have their  swords drawn and we even see sir harold  westerling with his blade against the  prince's chest if the show is to follow  the book this scene will end with daemon  bending the knee before the king what  you can't see unless you have the closed  captions on is a street performer asking  who will be heir the brother daughter or  prince aegon judging by these oddly  dressed figures and this magic performer  i wonder if some sort of street festival  is happening in town this magic dude is  also interesting because we just don't  know if he's using some kind of  pyrotechnic or if he's an actual magic  user to me he looks like some lowly  street performer but who knows the king  tells reinirro that her courtship is at  an end i guess she's had a year to look  for someone to marry after her father  told her in episode 3 she could have  anyone of her choosing it appears one of  these suitors could be a baratheon with  the baratheon emblem etched on the wall  here my guess is this is storm's end and  the manta ray near his right looks like  it may be the baratheon knight bormand  who we saw at the tournament in episode  1. perhaps one of the reasons rhaenyra  has not chosen a husband is that she's  secretly in love with her knight sir  kristen cole in the book it says quote  though many lords and nights sought her  favor the princess had eyes only for sir  kristen cole the young champion of the  kingsguard and her constant companion  things between the king and princess  have heated up and he expresses that she  is his political headache we get this  lovely shot is it king's landing or  somewhere else and here we have queen  allison holding her baby princess helena  you can see this takes place at king's  landing with the dragonpit visible in  the background and now for the main  drama of the episode otto approaches the  king with some salacious rumors but  knowing otto just how true these rumors  are we can't be sure the man is always  doing things to further house hightower  so it would make sense he may create  rumors to celebrate near his reputation  in order to get aegon named as air but  something does seem to happen here in  the shadows a hand on top of another in  an alleyway could this be the cloaked  daemon and rhaenyra the hand does have a  ring on it and daemon does wear a ring  on that finger rhaenyra also slipped out  during the night but we just can't tell  the book portrays two differing events  that could be these rumors otto refers  to one is from sept